-## v0.29.0: Accept verified native car records in the tuner
+## v0.30.0: Compact driving information HUD
+
+A small, click-through **Info HUD** appears below the upper-right launcher while the tools menu is closed. **F6** toggles it, or open **F8 → Info HUD**. It starts on and remembers only its display choice in this tab, separately from driving-tool profiles. Opening the menu hides the card until you close it. F7 returns control and F9 still stops driving assists; the HUD itself never enables them.
+
+- **Speed:** existing guarded native speed converted to **km/h**. Zero is shown only when sampled as zero. Unknown builds, invalid car data and paused/missing samples show **Unavailable**, never a guessed or multiplied speed. Older supported builds without verified speed telemetry also show Unavailable.
+- **Driver:** observed native AI/manual state, pending handoff, or the reason tools are waiting/paused. A selected AI switch is not called active by itself.
+- **Pace:** `req` is the current requested AI target factor; `ack` is a matching native acknowledgement, not measured vehicle speed. A newly selected factor does not reuse an old acknowledgement. Selected pace waits for AI; Drag and Drift retain native pace.
+- **Power:** `req` is the selected field multiplier; `set` reports guarded power-field application. It is not measured horsepower or a guaranteed speed increase. Paused, rejected and settling states stay distinct from application.
+
+The HUD is read-only and uses existing observations. Stop, manual takeover, blur, hidden tab, game exit, replacement boot and tuner suspension clear old display evidence. No new physics, AI, speed/power formula, native hook, network permission, tuning, game-save or profile-schema change is included. The complete v0.29 tuner/static-ride fix, online NOS correction, Street X, Drift, Drag and online tools remain together.
+
+**Verification:** 1,788 automated tests pass with no failures/skips/cancellations, including 20 focused HUD tests. A strict-CSP browser fixture is included, but Chromium could not launch because this environment disallowed its local process socket, including the elevated retry. Browser layout/fullscreen behavior and live game appearance remain unverified. No screenshot is presented as actual gameplay.
+
+## Retained v0.29.0: Accept verified native car records in the tuner
 
 The S20 report exposed an incorrect assumption: active car data is not always heap-allocated. The native game also embeds it in its fixed racer-record array. The tuner now accepts those exact native slots **only when the current car, record kind, active record count, race table and ride pointer all agree**. Arbitrary low addresses remain rejected; the existing heap path and all other safety checks remain.
 
